          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582782,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Influence on Chinese Culture</strong><br>\nLaozi's ideas have permeated many aspects of Chinese culture, influencing not only religion and philosophy but also politics, arts, and ecology. His teachings encourage living in balance with the cosmos, leading to sustainable practices and governance policies that align with the natural order.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Interpretations of Laozi's Work</strong><br>\nOver centuries, scholars have debated the interpretations of Laozi's work, often viewing it through lenses of philosophy, religion, and historical context. \"Tao Te Ching\" has been translated into many languages, reflecting its global appeal and the universal relevance of its teachings.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Taoism</strong><br>\nThe philosophy of Laozi laid the groundwork for Taoism, a religion and philosophy that deeply values harmony with the Tao. It emphasizes rituals and practices that align human behavior with the flow of the cosmos, promoting spiritual balance and ecological awareness.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "3b13867b-feab-4e2e-bfa2-fcc82e4dbff1"
            },
