            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Legacy of Tao Te Ching</strong><br>\nThe \"Tao Te Ching\" has inspired other works of literature, art, and philosophy. Its verses are often quoted in a variety of contexts, from environmental discussions to leadership seminars, reflecting the broad scope of Laozi's impact on both Eastern and Western thought.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Laozi's Mythical Status</strong><br>\nMyths surrounding Laozi describe him as a contemporary of Confucius and even as a supernatural figure. Some tales narrate his birth as an old man after his mother carried him for decades, symbolizing his extraordinary wisdom and connection to the Tao.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Modern Relevance</strong><br>\nToday, Laozi's teachings continue to resonate with those seeking a deeper understanding of the world. In an era of rapid change and technological advancement, his call for simplicity and a return to natural rhythms presents a compelling counter-narrative to modern complexities.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
